Subject: [PATCH] fork 000: fork base (fork-info command, build stamp)

What: new files cmd/holyarrs/fork_main.go (the fork's own first words on
the command line, forkCommand, the first one being fork-info, and the build
stamp main.forkBuild) and zz_fork_init.go (an init that runs a fork command
before main(); its name keeps it last among the package's init functions).

Why: fork/apply.ps1 and the home hub ask a program what it is (version,
flavour, patches, plugged-in site readers). Later patches register their
commands and names from init() instead of editing main() again.

Check: cmd/holyarrs/fork_check_000_test.go (the hook is there and sorts
last, the commands answer); apply.ps1 reads fork-info from holyarrs-mod.exe.

Upstream files edited: none (upstream's structure check caps main.go at
800 lines, and it is at 800).
